+## §778 — piste 2 swept, and why the gate was active
+
+Searched for projects sharing tokenade's goal rather than mining the existing
+folder. Everything the search surfaced — rtk, token-saver, tokensave, headroom,
+headroom-desktop, tokf, lean-ctx, token-optimizer — is ALREADY tracked in
+`competitors/`. Piste 2 returns nothing new on this query; the folder is
+comprehensive for the direct-competitor space. A future pass should aim at
+SUB-problems instead (log template mining, HTML extraction quality, secret
+redaction, tokenizer estimation), not at more direct competitors.
+
+**And the search answered §777's open question.** `tokenade search` refused:
+
+> your monthly token-savings quota is exhausted. Compaction is paused on this
+> machine until your quota resets on the 1st.
+
+So the licence gate is genuinely ACTIVE on this machine, which is exactly why
+`sync_gate_state` had retracted the scaffold blocks from the repo's own rules
+files. That was the feature working as designed, and the note in §777 stands
+confirmed rather than merely argued. It also means the measurements in §769-§777
+that used the INSTALLED binary were taken against a gated tool — they were
+timings and panics, which the gate does not alter, but any future measurement
+of SAVINGS on this machine would be worthless until the quota resets.
